                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "Today's Supreme Court ruling on Grants Pass v. Johnson restores the ability to limit homeless encampments in our streets, parks, and other public places. This allows our local communities to address homelessness in a common-sense and compassionate way that protects public health and safety while getting homeless individuals access to shelter and the assistance they need.\n\nHomelessness in California is a crisis and a tragedy that has only continued to get worse. I asked the Court to take this action because I believe our state can do so much better. Today is a new day: a chance to get this crisis under control, reclaim our public spaces, and help homeless individuals get back on their feet.",
